.TH VSCODE-NVIM-FOCUS 1 "2026-08-02" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vscode-nvim-focus \- publish leased Neovim focus ownership to VS Code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vscode-nvim-focus
.I claim|release SOURCE CYCLE SEQUENCE OBSERVED
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vscode-nvim-focus
posts an ordered focus update to the window-scoped
.B cgraf.termnav
adapter. Neovim integrations call it on focus changes and periodically while
focused. The adapter authenticates each update with a per-window token and
verifies that the client-reported process ancestry contains the active terminal
PID. A short lease ensures a killed editor, terminal, or tmux client cannot
leave terminal keybindings enabled indefinitely.
.PP
Inside tmux, claims are sent only through clients that are focused and display
the current
.B TMUX_PANE.
The socket is read from each tmux client process rather than inherited editor
state, so attaching a persistent session from another VS Code window does not
reuse the wrong window identity. The matching token is read from the same
client. A hidden pane releases its prior ownership, and continued polling lets
pane return or reattach recover without restarting Neovim. Releases are sent to
all attached client sockets and are ignored unless their source and focus cycle
own that window.
.PP
Outside tmux, the command uses the inherited
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_SOCKET
and
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_TOKEN.
Missing clients, partial credentials, or adapters fail closed without
diagnostics during normal focus publication.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B claim|release
Claim or release Neovim ownership.
.TP
.B SOURCE
Per-Neovim identifier containing only letters, digits, dot, underscore, colon,
or hyphen.
.TP
.B CYCLE
Monotonic focus cycle for the source.
.TP
.B SEQUENCE
Monotonic message sequence within the source.
.TP
.B OBSERVED
Monotonic host time in milliseconds used to reject delayed cross-source
messages.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_SOCKET
Owner-only Unix socket published into terminals by the local adapter.
.TP
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_TOKEN
Random per-window capability published with the socket and rotated whenever the
adapter restarts.
.TP
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_CURL
HTTP client used to post the update. Defaults to
.BR curl .
.TP
.B TMUX, TMUX_PANE
Identify the tmux server and pane whose focused clients are eligible to claim
ownership.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
At least one adapter accepted the update.
.TP
.B 1
An eligible adapter was found but the update failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 10
No eligible VS Code client or adapter was found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR termnav-navigate (1)
